<%#- ESCAPING: <%% emits runtime ERB into the generated view; a bare <% is
     consumed here at generation time. Never quote a closing ERB tag inside a
     comment — a literal one terminates the comment early and leaks the rest
     of this prose into the generated file.

     Emitted ONCE per app into app/views/shared/. The `--css=` marker below is
     how a later scaffold run detects a variant mismatch — keep it. Under
     --css=none the body is the scaffold-stock red block; the styled variants
     dress the same structure. -%>
<%%# locals: (record:) -%>
<%%# Shared error summary (--css=<%= css_variant %>), rendered by every
    scaffolded full-page form. The resource name comes off the record, so one
    file serves every scaffold. %>
<%% if record.errors.any? %>
  <div<%= css? ? %( class="#{css(:error_summary)}") : %( style="color: red") %>>
    <h2<%= css_attr(:error_summary_title) %>><%%= pluralize(record.errors.count, "error") %> prohibited this <%%= record.model_name.human.downcase %> from being saved:</h2>

    <ul<%= css_attr(:error_summary_list) %>>
      <%% record.errors.each do |error| %>
        <li><%%= error.full_message %></li>
      <%% end %>
    </ul>
  </div>
<%% end %>
